# Section 1: Security & Process Isolation Boundaries
- All file operations or tool calls generated by models must route through `core/security.py`.
- No Host Hand-Offs: Tools must never use raw host utilities (`xdg-open`, `cmd /c start`, or `open`) to process payloads.
- Strict Path Canonicalization: Limit reading/writing entirely to `<AppRoot>/sandbox_workspace/`. Instantly abort transactions if path tokens contain traversal operators (`..`) or absolute system paths.

# Section 2: Context Separation & Mode Rules
- Companion Mode and Storyteller Mode must be completely isolated pipelines. They can read from the `core/` and `storage/` primitives, but their files (`companion.py` and `storyteller.py`) must never cross-import.
- Companion Mode: Focused on conversational dialogue. Employs an 'Inner-Self' reflective hidden loop to evaluate conversational pacing and emotional context before outputting the final user-facing text.
- Storyteller Mode: Operates like an AI Dungeon narrative box. Continually loops text prose blocks, matches text keywords against `StoryCards` in the local `lorebook.py`, and appends the relevant details to guide subsequent generations.

